          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most commercial parking lots, a polymer-modified asphalt emulsion like Neyra PaveGuard or SealMaster NP-15 (coal tar) offers the best durability. For environmentally regulated areas, Crafco's coal-tar-free asphalt emulsion is the standard specification. The right product depends on traffic volume, chemical exposure, and local environmental regulations.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How often should commercial asphalt be sealed?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Commercial asphalt should be sealed every 3-5 years depending on traffic volume and the product used. High-traffic surfaces with fuel exposure (gas stations, fleet yards) may require resealing every 2-3 years. Coal tar products and polymer-modified emulsions typically last longer between applications than standard asphalt emulsion products.",
          },
