          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Coal tar provides superior chemical resistance to petroleum products and typically lasts 4-6 years vs 3-4 years for asphalt emulsion on commercial surfaces. However, coal tar is banned in multiple states and municipalities. Modern polymer-modified asphalt emulsions have significantly narrowed the performance gap, providing 4-5 year durability without the regulatory and environmental concerns of coal tar.",
