          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Material Costs</h3>
          <p>
            Standard commercial asphalt emulsion products run approximately <strong>$0.06–$0.10 per square foot</strong> in material cost at drum quantities. Premium polymer-modified products run <strong>$0.10–$0.16 per square foot</strong>. Refined coal tar products fall in the <strong>$0.08–$0.14 per square foot</strong> range. For a 50,000-square-foot commercial parking lot, material costs range from roughly $3,000 to $8,000 depending on product specification and whether the application is a maintenance recoat (lower coverage rate) or initial application on bare asphalt (higher coverage rate).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Total Contractor Costs</h3>
          <p>
            Professional commercial asphalt sealing typically runs <strong>$0.12–$0.25 per square foot</strong> fully installed, including materials, labor, surface preparation, and equipment. The wide range reflects differences in local labor markets, surface condition (heavily cracked lots requiring extensive crack filling cost more), and product specification. A 50,000-square-foot lot at the midpoint of this range costs approximately $9,000–$12,000 for a professional two-coat application.
