          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The ROI of Commercial Sealing</h3>
          <p>
            Commercial asphalt replacement costs between <strong>$2.50 and $5.00 per square foot</strong> depending on thickness, region, and base condition. A 50,000-square-foot parking lot replacement runs $125,000–$250,000. A properly maintained sealing program at 4-year intervals costs approximately $40,000–$50,000 over a 20-year period — roughly 20–40% of full replacement cost. The math is unambiguous: commercial sealing is among the highest-ROI property maintenance investments available, consistently delivering 10:1 or better returns in deferred pavement replacement costs.
          </p>

          <p>
            Beyond the direct pavement cost comparison, a well-maintained commercial lot communicates property quality to customers and tenants, reduces slip-and-fall liability on degraded surfaces, and preserves the underlying base layer from water infiltration damage that compounds repair costs over time. For property managers presenting maintenance budgets to ownership, the commercial sealing ROI argument is straightforward to quantify and compelling to approve.
